<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65824" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελάμ-πῡγος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>black-bottomed</i>,
			considered a mark of manhood, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				61
			</span></i>; a name of Heracles, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τοῖς
				ἐχθροῖς</span>
			<i>a very Heracles</i> to them, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				802
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.216
			</span></i>: prov., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τευ μ. τύχης</span>
			take care not to 'catch a Tartar', <i><span class="en">
				Archil.
				110
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of a kind of
			eagle, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πύγαργος</span>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
